+/* ioc-motion: two switches, 1 = upstream behaviour. Set before iocInit.
+ * AG_UCInitWrites: 1 (upstream) sends RS at controller creation (a reset: every
+ *   temporary setting back to its default, local mode) and each axis's forward
+ *   and reverse step amplitude (SU) at axis creation; 0 sends neither, so
+ *   creation sends MR (remote mode, without which TP, PH and every motion
+ *   command are refused) and VE only.
+ * AG_UCChannelUpstream: 1 (upstream) sends CC<n> before every command and every
+ *   axis poll and ignores its result, and reads TP as each axis's position.
+ *   The AG-UC8 refuses CC (error -6) while an axis of the selected pair moves
+ *   (user manual EDH0224En5010, 5.7), so a poll of an axis on another pair
+ *   reads the moving pair, and a move for it goes to the moving pair's axis of
+ *   the same number; and its step counter belongs to the axis slot (1 or 2),
+ *   shared by the four pairs (the first unit, 2026-10-29: 1PR10 on pair 1,
+ *   CC2 accepted, 1TP10), so every pair's axis n reads one position.
+ *   0 (selectPair):
+ *   - CC only when the pair changes, then TE. TE0: selected. TE-6: busy (the
+ *     selected pair steps; only it can). Anything else (a timeout, TE-5 in
+ *     local mode, another code, a malformed reply): the selection is unknown
+ *     and the axis shows a problem; it is learned again with CC? or, while a
+ *     slot steps (TS not 0), as refPair_, the only pair this driver moves.
+ *   - Counts: every change of a slot's TP is credited to refPair_'s axis in
+ *     that slot. refPair_ changes only after a CC was accepted (the pair it
+ *     leaves is idle, the counters carry over, the new pair has not moved),
+ *     and a move is sent only to refPair_, so no step is credited to the
+ *     wrong axis or lost, whatever reply goes missing. Each axis is 0 at IOC
+ *     start.
+ *   - Poll: busy, the axis is done (it cannot move). A timeout, a malformed
+ *     reply, an unknown selection or a refused CC (TE-5, another code): the
+ *     comms-error bit (COMM/INVALID on the record; it neither ends a move
+ *     nor clears the jog buttons) and done kept as last read, so a stepping
+ *     axis never reads done. The problem bit is not used for these.
+ *   - Move, home: refused unless the pair is selected; nothing sent, no
+ *     problem bit (the axis is idle and fine): the record ends the move with
+ *     MISS 1 and VAL != RBV. A target is computed from the axis's count read
+ *     just before.
+ *   - Stop never waits for a CC: with the selection known and another pair
+ *     selected, nothing on this pair moves and nothing is sent; known and
+ *     this pair, <axis>ST at once; unknown, <axis>ST at once only if this
+ *     axis's pair is refPair_ (the only pair that can be stepping), so a stop
+ *     for an idle axis of another pair never stops the stepping one.
+ *   - A failed resync is not retried for 1 s, so an unanswering controller
+ *     does not hold the poll lock (and a STOP behind it) for every axis.
+ * AG_UCJogAllowed: 1 (upstream) sends JA for the record's jog; 0 refuses it
+ *   (nothing sent; the problem bit for that one update, which clears the
+ *   record's jog buttons, cleared at the next poll). With AG_UCChannelUpstream
+ *   0 a jog refused because the pair is busy or unknown does the same. */
+volatile int AG_UCInitWrites = 1;
+extern "C" {epicsExportAddress(int, AG_UCInitWrites);}
+volatile int AG_UCChannelUpstream = 1;
+extern "C" {epicsExportAddress(int, AG_UCChannelUpstream);}
+volatile int AG_UCJogAllowed = 1;
+extern "C" {epicsExportAddress(int, AG_UCJogAllowed);}
